# Build/publish allowlist (Security Recommendation, Dimension 11: Attack-
# Surface Simplicity — "Add a build/publish allowlist so only intended
# assets deploy — no stray .git, source maps, or backups.")
#
# Everything below stays in the git repository (still visible on GitHub)
# but is excluded from the actual Vercel deployment, since none of it is
# part of the live application. Keeping the deployed surface to exactly
# the 8 app pages + assets + the one API route + SECURITY.md/security.txt
# means there's nothing else here for an attacker (or an accidental
# request) to reach.

# Assessment reports and docx exports — repo documentation, not app pages
docs/

# CI/repo configuration — not meaningful to serve
.github/
.gitleaks.toml
.env.example
scripts/

# Generic markdown, EXCEPT the two files the app actually links to
*.md
!SECURITY.md

# Defensive: never publish source maps or backup/version-control artifacts,
# even though none currently exist in this repo (see SURF-01 in the
# security findings — this is exactly the class of exposure that finding
# warns against).
*.map
*.bak
*.orig
.git/
